%%%
# A mixture of two bivariate normals

Spec §06 `ksuperpose` broadcasts weights and parameters together. Each
element of `mus` is a mean vector and each element of `covs` is a covariance
matrix. The outer vectors share one component axis. The mixture's variate
is the component variate, a vector of length two.

This is the first suite row whose mixture components are MULTIVARIATE. The
two clusters carry distinct full covariances, so neither the `mu` axis nor
the `cov` axis can be dropped without moving the number.
%%%
flatppl_compat = "0.1"

mus = [[-2.0, 1.0], [3.0, -1.0]]
cA = rowstack([[1.0, 0.3], [0.3, 1.0]])
cB = rowstack([[0.5, 0.0], [0.0, 2.0]])
covs = [cA, cB]

w = [0.3, 0.7]

% The weights sum to one and do not expand during broadcast.
mix = normalize(ksuperpose(MvNormal, w, mu = mus, cov = covs))

y = elementof(cartpow(reals, 2))
